// @check
// @error `as u8` propagates null out of the enclosing function, and there is none here — at module scope, use `as!` to trap or `as?` to take a nullable
// @error `as u8` propagates null, which the enclosing function cannot return (it returns i32) — use `as!` to trap instead, or `as?` to take the null here
// @error `as u8` narrows a number into 0..255, and i32 | null is a union — take the numeric arm first, then the range (`(x as! i32) as! u8`)
// @error `as` supports numeric conversions only
// @error unknown type `Bogus` in `as` cast
// @hint redundant type annotation: `fi32` is inferred as `i32`
// THE FOUR THINGS `x as u8` STILL REFUSES (D1587), each for the reason its neighbour in the
// cast family refuses it — the ruling gives `u8` the trio, not an exemption.
//
//   · A BARE `as` at MODULE SCOPE and in a non-nullable return: the failure is a `null` and
//     there is nowhere for it to go. Same sentences as `error-as-cast-bare-needs-suffix.vl`,
//     from the same `castPropagationFits` ladder, with `u8` as the quoted spelling.
//   · A UNION OPERAND: `as u8` narrows a NUMBER into a range, it does not pick an arm. The
//     arm ladder would hand back the arm's own `i32` with NO range test, so `x as! u8` over
//     an `i32 | null` holding 300 would answer 300 — the ruling's whole point, undone.
//   · A NON-NUMERIC operand: 0..255 is a range of numbers.
//   · `as Bogus` is the CONTROL: `u8` is admitted by NAME, only after resolution has failed,
//     so an ordinary unknown type in a cast keeps its own wording — and a program declaring
//     its own `type u8` resolves first and is unaffected (`builtin-type-name-user-type`).
//
// The ANNOTATION position is untouched and has its own fixture: `u8` is still not a value
// type there (`error-u8-storage-only.vl`), which is what makes the cast a narrowing into an
// `i32` rather than a conversion to a `u8`.
function fi32(x: i32): i32 { x }
const v = fi32(300)

const atModuleScope = v as u8
print(atModuleScope)

function intoNonNullable(x: i32): i32 {
  x as u8
}
print(intoNonNullable(v))

function fromUnion(x: i32 | null): i32 {
  return x as! u8
}
print(fromUnion(3))

const s = "x"
print(s as! u8)

print(v as! Bogus)
